1
00:07:12,631 --> 00:07:18,631
It's nothing personal.

2
00:14:25,263 --> 00:14:31,263
Terminator 2: Judgment Day is a action, thriller, science
fiction film directed by James Cameron.

3
00:21:37,894 --> 00:21:43,894
Ten years after the events of the original, a reprogrammed T-800 is sent back in
time to protect young John Connor from the shape-shifting T-1000.

4
00:28:50,526 --> 00:28:56,526
Together with his mother Sarah, he fights to stop Skynet
from triggering a nuclear apocalypse.

5
00:36:03,157 --> 00:36:09,157
The Terminator, played by Arnold Schwarzenegger.

6
00:43:15,789 --> 00:43:21,789
Sarah Connor, played by Linda Hamilton.

7
00:50:28,421 --> 00:50:34,421
John Connor, played by Edward Furlong.

8
00:57:41,052 --> 00:57:47,052
T-1000, played by Robert Patrick.

9
01:04:53,684 --> 01:04:59,684
Dr. Silberman, played by Earl Boen.

10
01:12:06,315 --> 01:12:12,315
Miles Dyson, played by Joe Morton.

11
01:19:18,947 --> 01:19:24,947
Starting in 1991, video games based on the Terminator film series have
been released throughout multiple console generations.

12
01:26:31,578 --> 01:26:37,578
The films generally focus on humans attempting to prevent the
rise of Skynet, an artificial intelligence.

13
01:33:44,210 --> 01:33:50,210
In the future, Skynet will wipe out most of humanity with
help from its army of Terminator machines.

14
01:40:56,842 --> 01:41:02,842
The first Terminator game was released for DOS in July 1991, and is
based on the original film, The Terminator (1984).

15
01:48:09,473 --> 01:48:15,473
Other games based on the first film and its sequel, Terminator 2:
Judgment Day (1991), were released over the next two years.

16
01:55:22,105 --> 01:55:28,105
Subsequent films also received game adaptations, and several
non-film based games have also been released.

17
02:02:34,736 --> 02:02:40,736
The film explores themes of man vs machine, cyborg,
shotgun, dystopia, moral ambiguity.

18
02:09:47,368 --> 02:09:53,368
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
